From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Subject: [PATCH] t880: convert tiled decoder output on the GPU

Use a bounded shared Panthor DMA-BUF for the negotiated tiled Y/UV extents.
Keep V4L2 plane offsets and stable linear VA presentation identity explicit.
A GLES shader reads the tiled bytes directly and writes linear NV12 planes;
wait for its completion fence before publishing pixels or requeueing input
storage. Preserve caller EGL state, immutable imports, original deadlines
and sticky failures. Do not fall back to CPU decoding or pixel copying.

Explicit upload/download APIs retain their CPU access semantics. The kernel's
separately requested linear V4L2 formats remain available to other clients.

